WEBVTT

NOTE Cue timings are estimated from sentence length and pauses in the audio.

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:04.532
Welcome to the Concilium Security Risk Brief for Friday, November thirteenth.

2
00:00:04.532 --> 00:00:13.533
Five minutes of security coverage from the last twenty four hours, to increase your situational awareness without decreasing your productivity.

3
00:00:13.533 --> 00:00:14.420
Here's what matters today.

4
00:00:14.420 --> 00:00:30.760
Today: Iran says it targeted a U.S. radar in Bahrain, new Houthi attacks on Saudi Arabia and fresh U.N. sanctions on the group, a rising death toll in eastern Congo, a deadly drone attack on Volgograd in Russia, and a grenade attack on a broadcaster in Cali, Colombia.

5
00:00:30.760 --> 00:00:32.817
We start with Iran and Bahrain.

6
00:00:32.817 --> 00:00:44.554
Reuters reports Iran's Revolutionary Guards said they targeted a U.S. early warning radar in Bahrain, the first such claim of an attack on American military assets in a Gulf country since early September.

7
00:00:44.554 --> 00:00:50.535
Al Jazeera reports the Guards called it retaliation for an attack on a telecommunications center in Iran.

8
00:00:50.535 --> 00:00:59.812
Arab News, citing Iran's state news agency, reports the southern port city of Sirik was hit by what Iranian officials called an enemy strike yesterday.

9
00:00:59.812 --> 00:01:00.699
Next, Saudi Arabia and Yemen.

10
00:01:00.699 --> 00:01:10.376
Houthi spokesmen claimed attacks on a military cargo plane at Sharurah airport, the Khamis Mushait air base and Aramco facilities, according to regional outlets including South24.

11
00:01:10.376 --> 00:01:19.932
Arab News reports the Saudi led coalition said it intercepted and destroyed two drones in the Riyadh region and another launched toward the Eastern Province.

12
00:01:19.932 --> 00:01:22.539
Arab News also reports the U.N.

13
00:01:22.539 --> 00:01:30.675
Security Council renewed its sanctions on Yemen and moved to cut off dual use components and chemicals the Houthis use to build drones and missiles.

14
00:01:30.675 --> 00:01:43.689
And the Institute for the Study of War says the Houthis launched an offensive in southeastern Lahij province on Wednesday, November eleventh, that likely aims to cut the road between Mokha and Aden.

15
00:01:43.689 --> 00:01:46.523
Turning to the Democratic Republic of the Congo.

16
00:01:46.523 --> 00:01:55.311
Radio Okapi reports at least thirty five people were killed and fourteen are missing after attacks attributed to the A D F rebels in Mambasa territory, Ituri province.

17
00:01:55.311 --> 00:02:00.426
Local outlets had first put the toll at twenty two on Wednesday.

18
00:02:00.426 --> 00:02:10.697
In Russia, Reuters reports four people were killed and two injured in a Ukrainian drone attack on an industrial zone in Volgograd, the deadliest attack on the city so far, regional governor Andrei Bocharov said.

19
00:02:10.697 --> 00:02:17.115
Separately, Reuters reports a Russian serviceman was killed when the car he was driving was blown up in St.

20
00:02:17.115 --> 00:02:20.017
Petersburg, investigators said.

21
00:02:20.017 --> 00:02:21.467
And in Colombia.

22
00:02:21.467 --> 00:02:30.230
On Wednesday, November eleventh, a grenade was thrown at the headquarters of broadcaster R C N in Cali, damaging the building, local media including R T C C Noticias reported.

23
00:02:30.230 --> 00:02:33.864
Colombia's press freedom foundation condemned the attack.

24
00:02:33.864 --> 00:02:37.170
Now a few quick notes by region.

25
00:02:37.170 --> 00:02:47.928
In South Asia, Dawn reports Balochistan police said two civilians were killed and three paramilitary personnel and thirteen civilians injured as security forces repelled an attack on the Kandawa post in Mastung.

26
00:02:47.928 --> 00:02:57.724
Dawn also reports Pakistan's military said thirty five militants were killed in Mir Ali, North Waziristan, and eight in Orakzai.

27
00:02:57.724 --> 00:03:11.015
In the Middle East, the Institute for the Study of War says Iran continues to claim that commercial vessels are striking naval mines along the U.S. backed route in the southern Strait of Hormuz, likely to undermine confidence in U.S. escort operations.

28
00:03:11.015 --> 00:03:22.234
In Europe, an update on the school bomb threats: The Record reports the threats sent to thousands of schools across Europe this week came from a compromised email account at a Taiwanese university.

29
00:03:22.234 --> 00:03:32.316
And Reuters reports Norway's security service says Russian intelligence could carry out sabotage in the coming year.

30
00:03:32.316 --> 00:03:42.256
In Africa, the International Committee of the Red Cross says it provided assistance to seventy two hundred people displaced by renewed hostilities in Ethiopia's Tigray region.

31
00:03:42.256 --> 00:03:50.178
And in cyber, Reuters reports the F B I says North Korean hackers stole more than four hundred million dollars using video images.

32
00:03:50.178 --> 00:03:57.717
The Record reports suspected Kazakhstan linked hackers used an artificial intelligence agent to help spy on Central Asian governments, according to new research.

33
00:03:57.717 --> 00:03:59.361
That's today's brief.

34
00:03:59.361 --> 00:04:08.965
These security developments come from government travel advisories and trusted analysts, curated by the Concilium Security Risk Management Team.

35
00:04:08.965 --> 00:04:17.079
The brief summarizes public reporting and isn't a substitute for your own risk assessment, so check the original source before making travel decisions.

36
00:04:17.079 --> 00:04:19.248
This brief is digitally narrated.

37
00:04:19.248 --> 00:04:20.197
Questions?

38
00:04:20.197 --> 00:04:23.752
Reach Concilium at info at concilium dot U.S.

39
00:04:23.752 --> 00:04:25.903
Thanks for listening, and stay safe.
